xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�X.��\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000K?\u0000\u0000customXml/item1.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�/%��\u0000\u0000\u0000U\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0018\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00008@\u0000\u0000customXml/itemProps1.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�$\u0007\u000f�\u0014\u0000\u0000��\u0001\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000wA\u0000\u0000word/numbering.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�v�G�\u000e\u0000\u0000l�\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000:V\u0000\u0000word/styles.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�k\u0013�\u0001\u0002\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u001de\u0000\u0000word/webSettings.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000��`�\u0002\u0000\u0000�\u000b\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Pg\u0000\u0000word/fontTable.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000J��r�\u0001\u0000\u0000�\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000,j\u0000\u0000docProps/core.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000C�\u000e�\u000e\u0002\u0000\u0000\u001a\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�l\u0000\u0000docProps/app.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000t?9z�\u0000\u0000\u0000(\u0001\u0000\u0000\u001e\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000<p\u0000\u0000customXml/_rels/item1.xml.relsPK\u0005\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0012\u0000�\u0004\u0000\u0000Br\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000","minutes_text":"LA VERNE YOUTH & FAMILY ACTION COMMITTEE\n  Minutes of the Regular Meeting\n  August 25, 2024\n\n1. A meeting of the Youth & Family Action Committee was called to order by Council\n  Member Wendy Lau at 5:00 p.m.\n\n  Executive Board Members present:\n\n  Executive Board\n  Wendy Lau, Council Member\n  Greg Palatto, BUSD\n  Denise Fisher, Resident\n  Don Kendrick, Resident\n\n2. Review of Minutes  Minutes for the March 26, 2024, meeting were approved.\n\n3. SRO Report  Student Resource Officer (SRO) Eduardo Burgos is\n  currently on leave however other officers from the La\n  Verne Police Department such as previously Student\n  Resource Officers have been filling in for him until his\n  return. They report that start of school has been going\n  smoothly.\n\n4. BUSD Report  Vice Principal Burgess provided an update on the Back\n  to School orientation, highlighting the success of the\n  Culinary group. The high school enrollment stands at\n  1,909 students, including 502 freshmen. BHS achieved a\n  record high AP testing pass rate of 74%, with an increase\n  of 134 tests from the previous year. The school has\n  celebrated three CIF championships and a state\n  championship last year. The arts programs are thriving,\n  and the girls' flag football team had a successful inaugural\n  game, with four captains receiving scholarship offers from\n  Marymount University in Virginia. Burgess also\n  mentioned the Bearcat Sessions held on the first day of\n  school to reinforce the values of being a Bearcat,\n  emphasizing respect and culture.\n\n5. Teach & Transform Grant  Tamara Baze provided an overview of her Artists Study\n  program at Roynon for 3rd graders, which emphasizes\n  the arts, including writing and creating art. The funding\n  for this program is allocated for books, videos, and\n  supplies that enable students to experiment with various\n  artistic mediums. The availability of these resources, not\n  included in the school’s budget, significantly enhances\n  the program and benefits the students. Additionally, the\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes June 25, 2024, page 2\n\n  students have the opportunity to visit the Norton Simon\n  Museum in the spring to experience art firsthand.\n\n6. Summer Lunch  Assistant City Manager JR Ranells shared that the\n  summer lunch program was highly successful, serving\n  over 2,700 lunches despite funding challenges after the\n  Tri-Cities Mental Health grant was not received. A total of\n  $16,000 was raised, with YFAC approving $5,000 for the\n  program. Donations came from various sources,\n  including many volunteer groups, vendors, city partners\n  and numerous individuals. BUSD will be taking over this\n  program moving forward and has approved the summer\n  lunch program for La Verne and San Dimas for future\n  years. The committee also discussed ways to thank the\n  people who generously donated to this years program.\n\n7. Fall Programs  Assistant City Manager JR Ranells shared the beginning\n  of the collaboration between teachers from BHS and\n  Damien on a utility box art project, where the City will\n  identify four boxes for painting by art classes.\n  Approximately $10,000 from the Reed Foundation will\n  fund this initiative. He has been in contact with the\n  Assistant City Manager of Claremont to gather insights\n  from their similar program. Additionally, Council Member\n  Lau suggested reaching out to the University of La Verne\n  for their inclusion in the project.\n\n8. Finance Updates  Assistant City Manager JR Ranells reminded the group\n  that there is approximately $10,000 of remaining funds\n  currently in the bank that could be used for future\n  programs and will bring more details back to the next\n  meeting.\n\n9. Public Comment  Denise Fisher shared that there was a Draft Day held at\n  Angel Stadium, where companies \"draft\" students based\n  on their prior presentations. Selected students then work\n  at the respective companies throughout the year. Wendy\n  mentioned that the University of La Verne offers a\n  \"Reach Program\" for high school students, allowing\n  them to present business ideas to local banks for\n  potential loans. JR Ranells will distribute a video about\n  Draft Day to the group. Peggy suggested placing\n  informative materials in bathrooms to help children\n  recognize potential signs of abuse and wrongdoing.\n  Wendy emphasized the district's strong commitment to\n  this issue and mentioned the need to effectively\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes June 25, 2024, page 3\n\n  communicate the various ways the district, Tri-City, and\n  other organizations support the community. JR also\n  highlighted the mandated reporting training provided to\n  city staff who work with children.\n\n10. Next Meeting  The next YFAC meeting was scheduled for September\n  24, 2024 at 5:00pm.\n\n11. Adjournment  The meeting was adjourned at 5:46 p.m.\n\nRespectfully submitted,\n\nErin Beilstein\nSenior Management Analyst"}